# LEB frontend (Blade)

## Baseline: generated pages

`php artisan make:crud {Module} {Entity} --web` generates the CRUD pages (`index`, `create`, `edit`, `show`, `_form`) in `resources/views/<module-kebab>/<entity-plural-kebab>/`. They are plain Blade with no JS, use the module's Actions and Queries through `<Entity>PageController`, and `@extends(config('blueprint.layout'))` (default `layouts/blueprint.blade.php`, created once). Generate them with the command; do not write them by hand. Change your layout or set `blueprint.layout`, or publish the stubs (`php artisan vendor:publish --tag=blueprint-stubs`).

- Dumb views; no business logic in Blade.
- Forms: CSRF; validation errors from the Store/Update requests.
- Show/hide feature UI with `@feature('key') ... @endfeature`; the route still needs `feature:key` middleware.

## Optional guidance for custom pages

- Page JS: jQuery only in page scripts; pass data via `window.PageData`.
- Heavy selects: Select2 + AJAX URL with load-more on scroll.
- Forms: disable submit after post; idempotency on critical submits.

If the project has a **frontend-views** skill, prefer that skill for detailed Blade rules.

## Languages

- Every visible string: `{{ __('English key') }}`; no hard-coded text, no string concatenation for sentences.
- RTL: rely on `<html dir>` from the layout; use logical CSS properties (`margin-inline-start`, `text-align: start`).
- Language switcher: `route('blueprint.locale', $locale)` for each of `config('blueprint.locales')`.
